11	// The sheet's people: a form that adds a person or edits the one opened, and the list with each
12	// person's claims, claimed and due-total, and the sheet's claimed total and due-total. A due-total
13	// is the sum of the person's open and settled claims' (already rounded) dues, 0.00 with none; a
14	// person whose grade in force on the sheet's today has no rate in force then has no due-total (n/a)
15	// unless one of those claims has a due. The sheet's due-total skips those with none.
16	// A person's grade is dated: an edit gives the grade from the form's grade-from date (the sheet's
17	// today unless another is entered), keeping the grades already given; the first grade applies from the
18	// beginning of time. A claim's due uses the grade in force on its date; the list shows the one in
19	// force on the sheet's today.
20	// Each person has a statement button: it records their due-total and binds their counting claims to
21	// their figures then; the row shows how many statements were taken, and the last one's due-total and date.
22	// A person can be retired from a date (the sheet's today when none is entered). Retired people are
23	// left out of the list unless "show retired" is on; their claims keep counting in every total.
24	// A person can be put on hold and taken off it again: while held, their open claims count in no
25	// live total (settled ones still do).
26	// Each person, and the sheet, shows how many of their counting claims are overdue (open, due by
27	// before the sheet's today) and those claims' dues added up (a claim with none adds nothing).
28	// A person can name other people on the sheet as patrons, one at a time from their row; the row shows
29	// their patrons' names (sorted) and their backing: the patrons' due-totals added up, skipping n/a.
30	@Component({
31	  selector: 'app-people',
32	  imports: [ReactiveFormsModule, PersonClaims],
33	  template: `
34	    <section aria-labelledby="people-heading">
